(3) LinkedList was suggested because Session objects/references needed to
be removed and added. LinkedList is a dynamic linear data structure which means
the size can shrink or enlarge at any time. If we used arrays, we would have to
do many methods into copying the array and making a new array to enlarge or shrink.
This would take too much time and too much repeated code for a simple add(Session) method.

Another solution to this would be to use ArrayList instead. Unlike LinkedLists,
ArrayLists have indices which can make it easier to access the first and last,
instead of iterating through the whole list. ArrayLists also are lower memory
than LinkedLists since you do not have to have pointer variables for the next item.
Similar to LinkedLists, ArrayLists are also resizeable and can produce the same, if
not a better/easier solution to write the methods.

